Lane

Lane 3: Structured Content Archetype Clustering

ML Task Type

Clustering (Unsupervised Learning)

Explanation

The goal of this lane is to group content pages with similar performance characteristics into meaningful clusters. Unlike classification, clustering does not use predefined labels. Instead, it identifies natural groups based on content performance metrics such as impressions, CTR, engagement rate, sessions, content age, and word count. These clusters help understand different content archetypes and support content management decisions.

2. Target or Proxy

Since clustering is an unsupervised learning problem, there is no target label.

Instead of predicting an output, the model groups pages using their observable performance features.

Features used for clustering
impressions_90d
sessions_90d
ctr
avg_position
engagement_rate
scroll_rate
content_age_days
word_count
ai_sessions_90d
content_type
freshness

The resulting clusters can later be interpreted as content archetypes such as:

Champions
Rising Stars
Hidden Gems
Stale Visible Pages
Low Engagement Pages
Weak Demand Pages
3. Success Metric

Because this is a clustering task, traditional metrics like accuracy are not applicable.

The quality of clustering will be evaluated using:

Silhouette Score
Davies–Bouldin Index
Cluster visualization
Cluster profiling and interpretation

A successful clustering model should produce well-separated and meaningful clusters that can support practical content review decisions.

