Observation

Each row in the dataset represents a single content page. The columns describe different performance metrics such as impressions, sessions, CTR, average position, engagement rate, content age, and word count. These features will be used to group similar pages into different content archetypes.

5. Why ML Beats a Fixed Rule Here

A fixed rule can identify only predefined conditions such as:

Content older than 180 days
CTR below a specific threshold
Low word count

However, content performance depends on multiple features interacting together.

A clustering algorithm can automatically discover hidden patterns among pages that cannot easily be described using manual rules. This allows the system to identify meaningful content archetypes and recommend different actions for different groups of pages.

Therefore, clustering provides a more flexible and data-driven solution than fixed rules.

